From eb4be4a50c8959068bf1aa9bf531ed2fd32836f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:57:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui, editor: code blocks and quotes in the composer look
 like blocks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.12 (ask 11). The composer is a Markdown buffer, so
fences and `>` quotes were already highlighted while typing (upstream);
they now also read as blocks, and a fence closes itself.

- Every row of a ``` fenced block (fences included; an unclosed fence
  runs to the end, as CommonMark reads it) and every run of quote lines
  gets a background and a 2 px left stripe, from theme colours. The
  rows are recomputed from the text on each Edited event
  (composer_blocks::scan_composer_blocks, a pure function).
- Typing ``` on a line of its own, outside a block, inserts the closing
  fence below and leaves the cursor after the opening one, where a
  language goes. It is its own undo step (finalize_last_transaction on
  both sides), so one undo takes the closing fence back and keeps what
  was typed. A fence that closes an open block is left alone, and so is
  anything after the backticks. It hooks EditorEvent::InputHandled,
  which only the platform input path emits: typed text, never a paste.

The editor part is small and additive: a per-type left border for row
highlights (Editor::set_row_highlight_left_border), carried by
LineHighlight.left_border and painted beside the row background. Kept
per highlight type so highlight_rows and its callers are untouched.

Tests: composer_blocks::tests, 6 unit (scan, fence_to_close) and 3 on
a real MessageEditor (fence closing + undo, a closing fence left alone,
block rows and their stripe, cleared when the text goes). Red seen with
the module registered but not wired: the 3 editor tests failed on the
missing highlight and the missing closing fence.

Zeo next proposal §6.39 (ask 63, 2026-11-16): a sent message keeps the
block look. It is a read-only MessageEditor filled by set_source_message
and never typed into, so the `Edited` path above never ran for it and the
look vanished once the message was sent. set_source_message now applies
it after setting the text. Test a_sent_message_keeps_the_block_look; Red
seen with the call removed.

Zeo next proposal §6.56 (ask 80, 2026-11-21): the look came and went.
The editor paints row highlights only in Full and Minimap (element.rs's
paint_background); the composer is Full while empty or expanded and
AutoHeight after the first message, and a sent message is always
AutoHeight, so the look showed intermittently and §6.39's never painted.
The tests had checked the data, not the paint. Now:
- paint_background paints, outside Full and Minimap, the row highlights
  that carry a left border -- Zeo's only -- grouped by bordered_row_runs
  (a pure function, tested); every other highlight stays unpainted there,
  as upstream.
- Fences follow CommonMark: three or more backticks or tildes; a backtick
  in a backtick fence's info string makes the line inline code (```` ```x``` ````
  used to open a block and flip every later one); a block closes on the
  same character, at least as long. Whether a typed ``` opens a block is
  read from the blocks above, not from counting fences.
- The look is refreshed on BufferEdited, not only Edited: the closing
  fence itself and insert_selections edit outside a typed transaction.
- No fence is closed while text is marked (a dead-key or IME composition).
- Code rows use element_hover, which shows on a sent message's bubble
  (editor_background); element_background barely did.
The proposal's "the empty last row of an open block is dropped" did not
reproduce: anchor_after at the end of the buffer is Anchor::Max, which the
row mapping keeps; a test guards it. Tests: 6 more in composer_blocks (Red
seen for 5 with the old code; the last-row one is the guard) and
element::tests::bordered_row_runs_keep_only_bordered_highlights_in_runs.
Proved on Xvfb: docs/assets/zeo-wave3-fixes-2026-11-21/ in the hub.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
